-- title:
--   Strata points for two classes agreeing at a prime
-- statement:
--   The statement is a single implication whose hypotheses carry the entire Čerednik–Drinfeld situation as explicit data; they are grouped below, each group naming the Lean hypotheses it contains, and the conclusion is then stated in full.
--
--   **Local arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a nonzero level $N$, with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), $r \nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O$ (`hdvr`) with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), this ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`); thus $Onr$ plays the role of the completed maximal unramified extension with its Frobenius. A monoid homomorphism `vdet` from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) which by `hvdet` takes the value $n$ at $g$ precisely when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion algebra and moduli schemes over $\mathcal O$.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ has $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is a division algebra over the completion at a finite place exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`), an element $\mu_\Lambda$ of $\Lambda$ with $\mu_\Lambda^2 = -r\bar r$ (`hμΛ`), a map $\mathrm{star}_\Lambda$ on $\Lambda$ with $\mu_\Lambda\,\mathrm{star}_\Lambda(x) = \bar x\,\mu_\Lambda$ (`hstarΛ`), and invertibility of $2$ in $\mathcal O$ (`h2`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a family `pt` of points attached to fake elliptic curves (two-dimensional abelian schemes with commutative relative group law, $\Lambda$-multiplication and level-$N$ data), such that `h𝒳` holds: $(\mathcal X, f, \mathrm{pt})$ is a coarse moduli space in the sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity of `pt` on points with values in algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a family `ptF` which is a fine moduli space for such curves equipped with a full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi$ in $\Lambda$ forming a level-twisting action (`hρ`). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`), and carrying `ptF` to `pt` (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, coarse moduli data $(\mathcal Y_\ell, g_\ell, \mathrm{ptT}_\ell)$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`) and degeneracy morphisms $d_0\ell, d_1\ell : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points forget the $\ell$-level (`hd₀`) and pass to the quotient by an $\ell$-level isogeny (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r$, $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion algebra and the group $\Gamma_t$.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); a finite idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that the intersection order `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); and the height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the unit group which by `hΓt` consists exactly of the units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at every finite place other than $v$. Families $s$ and $s_f$ indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ satisfying `hs` (four clauses): the adelic component of $s_f\ell$ at a place not above $r$ is $s\ell \otimes 1$, its component above $r$ is $1$, the product of the central idele of $\ell$ with $(s_f\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of `meetOrder R₁ n₁` at $\ell$ otherwise, and the reduced norm of $s\ell$ equals $\ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_{t\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s\ell\,\Gamma_t\,(s\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** The inclusion of $\mathbb Z$ in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`) and a map `coord` on $\Lambda$ with values in pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`: additive, unital, multiplicative for the twisted rule involving the Witt-vector Frobenius, injective, dense modulo every power of $r$, and trace-compatible). Over the residue ring $Onr/(\pi)$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0$, and `hA₀`, which says that $\theta_0$ identifies the relative group law of $A_0$ with $X_0$ and the $\Lambda$-action with the action read off from `coord`. Families $e, e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$, with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`, subject to: `hE1` (each $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to composing with multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational integral scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act as the corresponding multiplications), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a multiplication up to powers of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a central element $\varepsilon$ whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (the level-$n$ structure is moved by $e\gamma$ according to labels in $\Lambda$, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$), and `hE4` (over an algebraically closed field, every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny self-map of a fake elliptic curve pulled back from $A_0$ agrees, up to multiplications by powers of $r$, with some $e\gamma$). An order $R_2 \le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) absorbing $R_1$ after multiplication by powers of $r$ (`hR₂r`), acting on $A_0$ through $\hat e$ (`hê`), subject to `hE5a` (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of the level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unit, multiplicativity, and agreement with multiplication on integers), `hE5c` ($\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by the reduced norm of $x$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$) and `hE5e` (the joint version of `hE2` for $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously, with one common $g$).
--
--   **The formal moduli package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ to $Onr$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special with respect to the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`). A moduli package $MD$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`) and a family $\eta$ sending rigidified $\Phi$-objects over rings in which $r$ is nilpotent to $MD$-points, satisfying `hη` (three clauses: over Noetherian rings, $\eta$ identifies two admissible rigidified objects exactly when they are isomorphic; $\eta$ is compatible with base change of admissible objects; every $MD$-point is, on a Zariski cover by away-localisations, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$). A ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ which is injective and whose image is, after scaling by a fixed power $r^m$, exactly the image of $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). A family $eD$ of maps from the $G$-point functor of $MD$ (triples consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr \to B$, nilpotence of $r$ in $B$, and an $MD$-point) to the product of the functor $B \mapsto (Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B)$ with the Drinfeld functor `Omega K₀ π` of Deligne data, which is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), has the given structure map as first component (`hfstD`), transports the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into the twisted action of `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` — twisting the unramified structure map by $-v(\det g)$ and pulling the Deligne datum back along $g^{-1}$ — (`hGLD`), and carries $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist by $1$ on the first component (`hPiD`), $\pi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`); together with `hbdd`: for any pair of lattices $M' \subseteq M$ with $\pi M \subseteq M'$ there is a bound $N_\gamma$ such that over Artinian local Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with algebraically closed residue field and nilpotent $\pi$, every point whose Deligne datum lies in the edge chart of $(M',M)$ is $\eta(t)$ for an admissible rigidified object $t$ of level at most $N_\gamma$. Further, a ring homomorphism $\kappa : Onr/(\pi) \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`), and a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the special fibre: a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $aw, aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), morphisms $bw, bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving the level (`hBSwlev`), all over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`), and `hJOINTw`: one $g$ realises `hE2` for $\Gamma_t$ and in addition presents $aw$ followed by $bw$ by a central element whose image is $r^{k_w}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The period map $\Xi$.** A family $\Xi$ sending a fake elliptic curve with rigidification relative to $(r,\pi,A_0)$ over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and a structure map $\psi : Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B$ to a $G$-point of $MD$ over $B$, with `hΞleg` (over $B$ with no nontrivial idempotents the structure map of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullback of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (equality of values at two rigidified curves which are isomorphic and whose rigidifications admit a comparison up to multiplication by powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description: there are $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified $\Phi$-object $t$ with the given formal module, obtained by rig-transport from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, such that $\Xi$ equals the triple formed by the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$ and $\eta(t)$). An element $g_0$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ together with the two equivariance hypotheses `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds to acting by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some integer $c$) and `heqW` (over a ring in which $\bar r$ is invertible and which has no nontrivial idempotents, passing from a rigidified curve to its Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, with a comparison of rigidifications through $aw$ followed by $bw$, corresponds to acting by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   **The chart functor over $C$.** A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`) and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi_C : Onr \to C$. A functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras and a family $\mathrm{ptR}$ which, for $C$-algebras $S$ that are $\mathcal O$-algebras in a compatible tower and whose structure map $\psi_S$ is induced by $\chi_C$, attaches to a pair (full level-$n$ fake elliptic curve $u$, rigidification $\rho$ of $u$) an element of $PR(S)$, subject to `hR2` (compatibility with pullbacks of pairs along $C$-algebra maps), `hR3s` (surjectivity of $\mathrm{ptR}$), `hR3i` (over $S$ with no nontrivial idempotents, equal values force an isomorphism of the level structures together with a comparison of the rigidifications up to powers of $r$) and `hR1` (the converse implication). A natural transformation $\theta$ from $PR$ to the Deligne-datum functor (`hθnat`) with `hθ`: $\theta(\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho))$ is the Deligne-datum component of $eD(\Xi(u,\rho))$ pulled back along $g_0$. A family $\mathrm{toM}$ sending $PR(S)$ to $S$-points of the fibre product of $M$ and $\operatorname{Spec}C$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, natural (`hR0`) and compatible with $\mathrm{ptF}$ (`hR4`). Finally `hsh`: $PR$ satisfies unique Zariski gluing along covers given by a finite family generating the unit ideal; `het'`: for a surjection with square-zero kernel onto $S_0$ from a Noetherian $S$, every $PR$-point over $S_0$ together with a compatible lift of its $\mathrm{toM}$-point lifts uniquely to $PR(S)$; `hred`: the same unique lifting for the reduction modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$.
--
--   **The strata.** Schemes $X_d$ for $d \in \mathbb N$ with morphisms $\xi_d$ to the fibre product of $M$ and $\operatorname{Spec}C$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, locally of finite presentation (`hξ`) and formally unramified (`hunrξ`); families $\mathrm{pts}_d$ sending $T$-points of $X_d$ over $C$ to $PR(T)$, and $\mathrm{ptX}_d$ producing such $T$-points from pairs $(u,\rho)$ with $\rho$ of degree $d$ over a $C$-algebra $T$ in which the image of $\pi$ vanishes. These satisfy `hs0` (the existence of a $T$-point of $X_d$ forces the image of $\pi$ in $T$ to vanish), `hs1` ($\mathrm{toM}$ of $\mathrm{pts}_d(x)$ is $x$ followed by $\xi_d$), `hs2` (naturality of $\mathrm{pts}_d$ in $T$), `hx1` ($\mathrm{pts}_d \circ \mathrm{ptX}_d = \mathrm{ptR}$), `hx2` (naturality of $\mathrm{ptX}_d$ under pullbacks of pairs), `hx3` (every $T$-point of $X_d$ is of the form $\mathrm{ptX}_d(u,\rho)$), `hx4` (two values of $\mathrm{ptX}_d$ coincide if and only if the level structures are isomorphic and the rigidifications admit an exact comparison, with no correction by powers of $r$) and `hs4` (a class $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)$ lies in the image of $\mathrm{pts}_d$ exactly when $u$ carries a rigidification of degree $d$ with the same $\mathrm{ptR}$-class). Lastly an element $g_\pi$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ whose matrix is the diagonal matrix with entries $\pi$ and $1$ (`hgπ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above: for every Noetherian ring $A$ that is an algebra over $C$ and over $\mathcal O$ with compatible tower, in which the image of $\pi$ vanishes, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $A$, every localisation $L$ of $A$ at $\mathfrak p$ (a $C$-algebra with compatible tower over $A$), and all $x, x' \in PR(A)$ whose images in $PR(L)$ along the structural map coincide, there exist a natural number $d$ and two points $y, y'$ of $X_d$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ relative to $\operatorname{Spec}C$ — that is, morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}A \to X_d$ whose composite with $\xi_d$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}C$ is the morphism induced by $C \to A$ — such that all three of the following hold: $\mathrm{pts}_d(y) = x$; $\mathrm{pts}_d(y') = x'$; and the two composites of $\operatorname{Spec}L \to \operatorname{Spec}A$ with $y$ and with $y'$ are equal.
--
--   A spreading-out step inside the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: two classes of rigidified fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure over a $\pi$-killed Noetherian base that become equal after localising at a prime are realised by points of one and the same isogeny-degree stratum $X_d$, still agreeing over the localisation. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_away_map_eq_of_atPrime_map_eq_of_rigidifiedToG`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_away_map_eq_of_atPrime_map_eq_of_rigidifiedToG), where the agreement is propagated from the local ring to a neighbourhood.
